==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suf|en|abuse|age}}.

First appeared in {{inh|en|enm|-}}, c. 1450–1475, meaning “sexual misconduct”: cf. {{m|en|abuse|t=forcing of undesired sexual activity}}.<ref>{{R:MED Online|abūsaǧe|n|MED239.5}}</ref> Later in the 16th century, a general synonym of {{m|en|abuse}}. The word was partly repopularized after the appearance of a grammar titled ''[[w:Usage and Abusage|Usage and Abusage: A Guide to Good English]]'' in 1942.

